IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XIX -- INVESTIGATION (ss 229 to 237).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes anyone's point of view.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE READS THE TEXT.
--   * A judgment the Act hands to the court or to the Director ("if it appears to the court that ...",
--     "if the Director is satisfied that ...") is a plain BOOLEAN input named for the judgment; it is
--     never worked out here. The facts underneath it are the court's to find.
--   * Where the Act names a party (a security holder, the Director) the party is a constructor of the
--     keel's `Party`.
--   * A duty is a decision: "has complied" is true when no duty arose or the thing was done. A deadline,
--     where the Act gives one, is a DATE worked out with the keel's time-limit rules.
--   * A list of orders "the court may make" is an enumeration with one rule over the kind.
--   * A fact about a provision outside this piece is a plain input with a comment
--     "out of range: section N (piece X)".

§ `Part XIX -- Investigation`

§§ `s 229 -- application for an investigation`

-- "A security holder or the Director" is the whole list of applicants. "Ex parte or on such notice as the
-- court may require" is how the application is made (the court decides the notice), not a condition.
-- src:2864 | 229 (1) A security holder or the Director may apply, ex parte or on such notice as the court may require, to a court having jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office for an order directing an investigation to be made of the corporation and any of its affiliated corporations.
@ref CBCA s 229(1) (src:2864)
GIVEN applicant IS A Party
      `the court has jurisdiction in the place of the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for an order directing an investigation within s 229(1)` IF
        (    applicant EQUALS `a security holder`
         OR  applicant EQUALS `the Director`)
    AND `the court has jurisdiction in the place of the registered office`

-- The four grounds are alternatives ("or"); each is a judgment of the court ("it appears to the court").
-- src:2866 | (2) If, on an application under subsection (1), it appears to the court that
-- src:2867 | (a) the business of the corporation or any of its affiliates is or has been carried on with intent to defraud any person,
-- src:2868 | (b) the business or affairs of the corporation or any of its affiliates are or have been carried on or conducted, or the powers of the directors are or have been exercised in a manner that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or that unfairly disregards the interests of a security holder,
-- src:2869 | (c) the corporation or any of its affiliates was formed for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose or is to be dissolved for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose, or
-- src:2870 | (d) persons concerned with the formation, business or affairs of the corporation or any of its affiliates have in connection therewith acted fraudulently or dishonestly,
-- src:2871 | the court may order an investigation to be made of the corporation and any of its affiliated corporations.
@ref CBCA s 229(2) (src:2866-2871)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 229(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the business of the corporation or an affiliate is or has been carried on with intent to defraud any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the business or affairs of the corporation or an affiliate are or have been carried on or conducted, or the powers of the directors are or have been exercised, in a manner that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or that unfairly disregards the interests of a security holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the corporation or an affiliate was formed or is to be dissolved for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that persons concerned with the formation, business or affairs of the corporation or an affiliate have acted fraudulently or dishonestly in connection with them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order an investigation within s 229(2)` IF
        `an application has been made under subsection 229(1)`
    AND (    `it appears to the court that the business of the corporation or an affiliate is or has been carried on with intent to defraud any person`
         OR  `it appears to the court that the business or affairs of the corporation or an affiliate are or have been carried on or conducted, or the powers of the directors are or have been exercised, in a manner that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or that unfairly disregards the interests of a security holder`
         OR  `it appears to the court that the corporation or an affiliate was formed or is to be dissolved for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose`
         OR  `it appears to the court that persons concerned with the formation, business or affairs of the corporation or an affiliate have acted fraudulently or dishonestly in connection with them`)

-- Hohfeld: the security holder bears the duty to give notice; the Director holds the claim to it and the
-- liberty-right to appear. Written once each, below. The Director who applies gives notice to nobody.
-- src:2873 | (3) A security holder who makes an application under subsection (1) shall give the Director reasonable notice thereof and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 229(3) (src:2873)
GIVEN applicant IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant must give the Director reasonable notice within s 229(3)` IF
    applicant EQUALS `a security holder`

-- src:2873 | (3) A security holder who makes an application under subsection (1) shall give the Director reasonable notice thereof and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 229(3) (src:2873)
GIVEN applicant IS A Party
      `the Director was given reasonable notice of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant has complied with the duty to notify the Director within s 229(3)` IF
        (NOT `the applicant must give the Director reasonable notice within s 229(3)` applicant)
    OR  `the Director was given reasonable notice of the application`

-- src:2873 | (3) A security holder who makes an application under subsection (1) shall give the Director reasonable notice thereof and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 229(3) (src:2873)
GIVEN `a security holder has made an application under subsection 229(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director is entitled to appear and be heard within s 229(3)` IF
    `a security holder has made an application under subsection 229(1)`

-- "Is not required": the Act itself imposes no requirement; it is not a permission to omit one.
-- src:2875 | (4) An applicant under this section is not required to give security for costs.
@ref CBCA s 229(4) (src:2875)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an applicant under s 229 is required to give security for costs within s 229(4)` MEANS FALSE

-- "An ex parte application under this section shall be heard in camera": the hearing is in camera
-- exactly when the application is ex parte.
-- src:2877 | (5) An ex parte application under this section shall be heard in camera.
@ref CBCA s 229(5) (src:2877)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application must be heard in camera within s 229(5)` IF
    `the application is made ex parte`

-- The prohibition reaches "ex parte proceedings under this section" only; the two ways round it are
-- alternatives ("or"): the court authorizes, or the corporation being investigated consents in writing.
-- src:2879 | (6) No person may publish anything relating to ex parte proceedings under this section except with the authorization of the court or the written consent of the corporation being investigated.
@ref CBCA s 229(6) (src:2879)
GIVEN `the proceedings are ex parte proceedings under s 229` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has authorized the publication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation being investigated has consented in writing to the publication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `publishing anything relating to the proceedings is permitted within s 229(6)` IF
        (NOT `the proceedings are ex parte proceedings under s 229`)
    OR  `the court has authorized the publication`
    OR  `the corporation being investigated has consented in writing to the publication`

§§ `s 230 -- powers of the court in an investigation`

-- The twelve paragraphs are the kinds of order the court may make; "any order it thinks fit including,
-- without limiting the generality of the foregoing" opens the list, so a thirteenth kind stands for
-- every other order. The condition is the same for every kind: the order is made in connection with an
-- investigation under this Part.
-- src:2881 | 230 (1) In connection with an investigation under this Part, the court may make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:2882 | (a) an order to investigate;
-- src:2883 | (b) an order appointing an inspector, who may be the Director, fixing the remuneration of an inspector, and replacing an inspector;
-- src:2884 | (c) an order determining the notice to be given to any interested person, or dispensing with notice to any person;
-- src:2885 | (d) an order authorizing an inspector to enter any premises in which the court is satisfied there might be relevant information, and to examine any thing and make copies of any document or record found on the premises;
-- src:2886 | (e) an order requiring any person to produce documents or records to the inspector;
-- src:2887 | (f) an order authorizing an inspector to conduct a hearing, administer oaths, and examine any person on oath, and prescribing rules for the conduct of the hearing;
-- src:2888 | (g) an order requiring any person to attend a hearing conducted by an inspector and to give evidence on oath;
-- src:2889 | (h) an order giving directions to an inspector or any interested person on any matter arising in the investigation;
-- src:2890 | (i) an order requiring an inspector to make an interim or final report to the court;
-- src:2891 | (j) an order determining whether a report of an inspector should be published and, if so, ordering the Director to publish the report in whole or in part or to send copies to any person the court designates;
-- src:2892 | (k) an order requiring an inspector to discontinue an investigation; and
-- src:2893 | (l) an order requiring the corporation to pay the costs of the investigation.
@ref CBCA s 230(1) (src:2881-2893)
DECLARE `Kind of order in connection with an investigation (s 230(1))` IS ONE OF
    `an order to investigate (s 230(1)(a))`
    `an order appointing, remunerating or replacing an inspector (s 230(1)(b))`
    `an order fixing notice to an interested person or dispensing with it (s 230(1)(c))`
    `an order authorizing an inspector to enter premises and copy documents (s 230(1)(d))`
    `an order requiring any person to produce documents or records to the inspector (s 230(1)(e))`
    `an order authorizing an inspector to hold a hearing and examine on oath (s 230(1)(f))`
    `an order requiring any person to attend a hearing and give evidence on oath (s 230(1)(g))`
    `an order giving directions to an inspector or an interested person (s 230(1)(h))`
    `an order requiring an inspector to report to the court (s 230(1)(i))`
    `an order on whether and how an inspector's report is published (s 230(1)(j))`
    `an order requiring an inspector to discontinue the investigation (s 230(1)(k))`
    `an order requiring the corporation to pay the costs of the investigation (s 230(1)(l))`
    `any other order the court thinks fit (s 230(1))`

-- src:2881 | 230 (1) In connection with an investigation under this Part, the court may make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
@ref CBCA s 230(1) (src:2881)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of order in connection with an investigation (s 230(1))`
      `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order of the kind within s 230(1)` IF
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an order to investigate (s 230(1)(a))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order appointing, remunerating or replacing an inspector (s 230(1)(b))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order fixing notice to an interested person or dispensing with it (s 230(1)(c))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order authorizing an inspector to enter premises and copy documents (s 230(1)(d))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order requiring any person to produce documents or records to the inspector (s 230(1)(e))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order authorizing an inspector to hold a hearing and examine on oath (s 230(1)(f))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order requiring any person to attend a hearing and give evidence on oath (s 230(1)(g))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order giving directions to an inspector or an interested person (s 230(1)(h))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order requiring an inspector to report to the court (s 230(1)(i))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order on whether and how an inspector's report is published (s 230(1)(j))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order requiring an inspector to discontinue the investigation (s 230(1)(k))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `an order requiring the corporation to pay the costs of the investigation (s 230(1)(l))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`
    WHEN `any other order the court thinks fit (s 230(1))` THEN `the order is made in connection with an investigation under Part XIX`

-- The duty is the inspector's; "has complied" is true when there was no report to send or a copy was sent.
-- src:2895 | (2) An inspector shall send to the Director a copy of every report made by the inspector under this Part.
@ref CBCA s 230(2) (src:2895)
GIVEN `the inspector has made a report under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspector has sent the Director a copy of the report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inspector has complied with the duty to send the Director a copy of a report within s 230(2)` IF
        (NOT `the inspector has made a report under Part XIX`)
    OR  `the inspector has sent the Director a copy of the report`

§§ `s 231 -- powers of an inspector`

-- An inspector has no power of the Act's own: only "the powers set out in the order appointing him".
-- src:2897 | 231 (1) An inspector under this Part has the powers set out in the order appointing him.
@ref CBCA s 231(1) (src:2897)
GIVEN `the power is set out in the order appointing the inspector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an inspector has the power within s 231(1)` IF
    `the power is set out in the order appointing the inspector`

-- The permission is the inspector's; all four conditions must hold (one "and" list, no "or").
-- src:2899 | (2) In addition to the powers set out in the order appointing him, an inspector appointed to investigate a corporation may furnish to, or exchange information and otherwise cooperate with, any public official in Canada or elsewhere who is authorized to exercise investigatory powers and who is investigating, in respect of the corporation, any allegation of improper conduct that is the same as or similar to the conduct described in subsection 229(2).
@ref CBCA s 231(2) (src:2899)
GIVEN `the inspector was appointed to investigate a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is a public official in Canada or elsewhere authorized to exercise investigatory powers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is investigating the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is investigating an allegation of improper conduct that is the same as or similar to the conduct described in subsection 229(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an inspector may furnish information to or exchange it with the official within s 231(2)` IF
        `the inspector was appointed to investigate a corporation`
    AND `the recipient is a public official in Canada or elsewhere authorized to exercise investigatory powers`
    AND `the recipient is investigating the corporation`
    AND `the recipient is investigating an allegation of improper conduct that is the same as or similar to the conduct described in subsection 229(2)`

-- Hohfeld: the interested person holds the claim; the inspector bears the duty. "On request" is the trigger.
-- src:2901 | (3) An inspector shall on request produce to an interested person a copy of any order made under subsection 230(1).
@ref CBCA s 231(3) (src:2901)
GIVEN `the person is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has asked the inspector for a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was made under subsection 230(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inspector must produce a copy of the order within s 231(3)` IF
        `the person is an interested person`
    AND `the person has asked the inspector for a copy`
    AND `the order was made under subsection 230(1)`

§§ `s 232 -- hearings and counsel`

-- src:2903 | 232 (1) Any interested person may apply to the court for an order that a hearing conducted by an inspector under this Part be heard in camera and for directions on any matter arising in the investigation.
@ref CBCA s 232(1) (src:2903)
GIVEN `the person is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hearing is conducted by an inspector under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an interested person may apply to the court for an in camera hearing and directions within s 232(1)` IF
        `the person is an interested person`
    AND `the hearing is conducted by an inspector under Part XIX`

-- The two limbs are alternatives ("or"): a person whose conduct is being investigated, or a person being examined.
-- src:2905 | (2) A person whose conduct is being investigated or who is being examined at a hearing conducted by an inspector under this Part has a right to be represented by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 232(2) (src:2905)
GIVEN `the person's conduct is being investigated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is being examined at a hearing conducted by an inspector under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has a right to be represented by counsel within s 232(2)` IF
        `the person's conduct is being investigated`
    OR  `the person is being examined at a hearing conducted by an inspector under Part XIX`

§§ `s 233 -- criminating statements`

-- "No person is excused ... by reason only that the evidence tends to criminate": the Act removes the
-- excuse; it does not add one.
-- src:2907 | 233 No person is excused from attending and giving evidence and producing documents and records to an inspector under this Part by reason only that the evidence tends to criminate that person or subject that person to any proceeding or penalty, but no such evidence shall be used or is receivable against that person in any proceeding thereafter instituted against that person under an Act of Parliament, other than a prosecution under section 132 of the Criminal Code for perjury in giving the evidence or a prosecution under section 136 of the Criminal Code in respect of the evidence.
@ref CBCA s 233 (src:2907)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person is excused from giving evidence by reason only that it tends to criminate within s 233` MEANS FALSE

-- The use bar: evidence given under compulsion may not be used against the person in a proceeding
-- instituted afterwards under an Act of Parliament, other than a perjury prosecution (Criminal Code
-- s 132) or a prosecution under Criminal Code s 136 in respect of the evidence. A proceeding that is not
-- under an Act of Parliament is not touched by s 233, which is a different answer from "barred".
-- src:2907 | 233 No person is excused from attending and giving evidence and producing documents and records to an inspector under this Part by reason only that the evidence tends to criminate that person or subject that person to any proceeding or penalty, but no such evidence shall be used or is receivable against that person in any proceeding thereafter instituted against that person under an Act of Parliament, other than a prosecution under section 132 of the Criminal Code for perjury in giving the evidence or a prosecution under section 136 of the Criminal Code in respect of the evidence.
@ref CBCA s 233 (src:2907)
DECLARE `Use of evidence given to an inspector (s 233)` IS ONE OF
    `s 233 bars the use of the evidence against the person`
    `s 233 does not bar the use of the evidence against the person`

-- src:2907 | 233 No person is excused from attending and giving evidence and producing documents and records to an inspector under this Part by reason only that the evidence tends to criminate that person or subject that person to any proceeding or penalty, but no such evidence shall be used or is receivable against that person in any proceeding thereafter instituted against that person under an Act of Parliament, other than a prosecution under section 132 of the Criminal Code for perjury in giving the evidence or a prosecution under section 136 of the Criminal Code in respect of the evidence.
@ref CBCA s 233 (src:2907)
GIVEN `the evidence was given to an inspector under Part XIX and tends to criminate the person or subject the person to a proceeding or penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding was instituted against the person after the evidence was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a prosecution under section 132 of the Criminal Code for perjury in giving the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a prosecution under section 136 of the Criminal Code in respect of the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Use of evidence given to an inspector (s 233)`
DECIDE `the use of the evidence within s 233` IS
    IF      `the evidence was given to an inspector under Part XIX and tends to criminate the person or subject the person to a proceeding or penalty`
        AND `the proceeding was instituted against the person after the evidence was given`
        AND `the proceeding is under an Act of Parliament`
        AND (NOT `the proceeding is a prosecution under section 132 of the Criminal Code for perjury in giving the evidence`)
        AND (NOT `the proceeding is a prosecution under section 136 of the Criminal Code in respect of the evidence`)
    THEN `s 233 bars the use of the evidence against the person`
    ELSE `s 233 does not bar the use of the evidence against the person`

§§ `s 234 -- absolute privilege`

-- The maker is "an inspector or any other person": the maker does not matter, only that the statement or
-- report was made in an investigation under this Part.
-- src:2909 | 234 Any oral or written statement or report made by an inspector or any other person in an investigation under this Part has absolute privilege.
@ref CBCA s 234 (src:2909)
GIVEN `the statement or report was made in an investigation under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement or report has absolute privilege within s 234` IF
    `the statement or report was made in an investigation under Part XIX`

§§ `s 235 -- information respecting ownership and control`

-- The power is the Director's, on the Director's own satisfaction and belief (both are the Director's
-- judgments, taken as inputs). The Parts and the regulation power named are out of this piece.
-- src:2911 | 235 (1) If the Director is satisfied that, for the purposes of Part XI, XIII or XVII, or for the purposes of enforcing any regulation made under section 174, there is reason to inquire into the ownership or control of a security of a corporation or any of its affiliates, the Director may require any person that the Director reasonably believes has or has had an interest or right in the security or acts or has acted on behalf of a person with such an interest or right to report to him or her or to any person the Director designates
@ref CBCA s 235(1) (src:2911)
GIVEN `the Director is satisfied that there is reason to inquire into the ownership or control of a security of a corporation or any of its affiliates for the purposes of Part XI, XIII or XVII or of enforcing a regulation made under section 174` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: Parts XI and XIII (piece cb3), Part XVII and section 174 (piece cb4)
      `the Director reasonably believes that the person has or has had an interest or right in the security or acts or has acted on behalf of a person with such an interest or right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may require the person to report within s 235(1)` IF
        `the Director is satisfied that there is reason to inquire into the ownership or control of a security of a corporation or any of its affiliates for the purposes of Part XI, XIII or XVII or of enforcing a regulation made under section 174`
    AND `the Director reasonably believes that the person has or has had an interest or right in the security or acts or has acted on behalf of a person with such an interest or right`

-- What the person must report: both (a) and (b), joined by "and".
-- src:2912 | (a) information that the person has or can reasonably be expected to obtain as to present and past interests or rights in the security; and
-- src:2913 | (b) the names and addresses of the persons with such an interest or right and of any person who acts or has acted in relation to the security on their behalf.
@ref CBCA s 235(1) (src:2912-2913)
GIVEN `the person reported the information that the person has or can reasonably be expected to obtain as to present and past interests or rights in the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person reported the names and addresses of the persons with such an interest or right and of any person who acts or has acted in relation to the security on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has made the report required within s 235(1)` IF
        `the person reported the information that the person has or can reasonably be expected to obtain as to present and past interests or rights in the security`
    AND `the person reported the names and addresses of the persons with such an interest or right and of any person who acts or has acted in relation to the security on their behalf`

-- "Deemed to have an interest or right" if any of (a), (b), (c) ("or").
-- src:2915 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a person is deemed to have an interest or right in a security if
-- src:2916 | (a) the person has a right to vote or to acquire or dispose of the security or any interest or right in it;
-- src:2917 | (b) the person’s consent is necessary for the exercise of the rights or privileges of any other person with an interest or right in the security; or
-- src:2918 | (c) any other person with an interest or right in the security can be required or is accustomed to exercise rights or privileges attached to the security in accordance with the person’s instructions.
@ref CBCA s 235(2) (src:2915-2918)
GIVEN `the person has a right to vote or to acquire or dispose of the security or any interest or right in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's consent is necessary for the exercise of the rights or privileges of any other person with an interest or right in the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other person with an interest or right in the security can be required or is accustomed to exercise rights or privileges attached to the security in accordance with the person's instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is deemed to have an interest or right in the security within s 235(2)` IF
        `the person has a right to vote or to acquire or dispose of the security or any interest or right in it`
    OR  `the person's consent is necessary for the exercise of the rights or privileges of any other person with an interest or right in the security`
    OR  `any other person with an interest or right in the security can be required or is accustomed to exercise rights or privileges attached to the security in accordance with the person's instructions`

-- The Director's duty to publish: both conditions ("and").
-- src:2920 | (3) The Director shall publish in a publication generally available to the public the particulars of information obtained by the Director under this section, if the particulars
-- src:2921 | (a) are required to be disclosed by this Act or the regulations; and
-- src:2922 | (b) have not previously been so disclosed.
@ref CBCA s 235(3) (src:2920-2922)
GIVEN `the particulars were obtained by the Director under section 235` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars are required to be disclosed by this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars have not previously been so disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director must publish the particulars within s 235(3)` IF
        `the particulars were obtained by the Director under section 235`
    AND `the particulars are required to be disclosed by this Act or the regulations`
    AND `the particulars have not previously been so disclosed`

-- Offence: failing to comply with a requirement made of the person under s 235(1).
-- src:2924 | (4) A person who fails to comply with this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 235(4) (src:2924)
GIVEN `a requirement was made of the person under subsection 235(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person complied with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence within s 235(4)` IF
        `a requirement was made of the person under subsection 235(1)`
    AND (NOT `the person complied with the requirement`)

-- The five-thousand-dollar fine and six-month term are ceilings; the court sets the sentence.
-- src:2924 | (4) A person who fails to comply with this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 235(4) (src:2924)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment on summary conviction`
`the most the court may impose within s 235(4)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment on summary conviction` WITH
        `largest fine in dollars` IS 5_000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS 6
        `fine and imprisonment may both be imposed` IS TRUE

-- A director or officer is a party to and guilty of the offence if the body corporate commits it and the
-- director or officer knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in it. "Whether or not the body
-- corporate has been prosecuted or convicted" removes any condition about the body corporate's
-- prosecution, so no input about it is taken.
-- src:2926 | (5) Where a body corporate commits an offence under subsection (4), any director or officer of the body corporate who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both, whether or not the body corporate has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref CBCA s 235(5) (src:2926)
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 235(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director or officer is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 235(5)` IF
        `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 235(4)`
    AND `the person is a director or officer of the body corporate`
    AND `the person knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence`

-- src:2926 | (5) Where a body corporate commits an offence under subsection (4), any director or officer of the body corporate who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both, whether or not the body corporate has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref CBCA s 235(5) (src:2926)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment on summary conviction`
`the most the court may impose on a director or officer within s 235(5)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment on summary conviction` WITH
        `largest fine in dollars` IS 5_000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS 6
        `fine and imprisonment may both be imposed` IS TRUE

§§ `s 236 -- solicitor-client privilege`

-- "Nothing in this Part shall be construed as affecting" the privilege: the Part does not affect it.
-- src:2928 | 236 Nothing in this Part shall be construed as affecting solicitor-client privilege or, in Quebec, the professional secrecy of advocates and notaries.
@ref CBCA s 236 (src:2928)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Part XIX affects solicitor-client privilege or professional secrecy within s 236` MEANS FALSE

§§ `s 237 -- inquiries by the Director`

-- src:2930 | 237 (1) The Director may make inquiries of any person relating to compliance with this Act and may, as part of any inquiry, require the person to provide any records or other documents or information.
@ref CBCA s 237(1) (src:2930)
GIVEN `the inquiry relates to compliance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may make the inquiry and require records within s 237(1)` IF
    `the inquiry relates to compliance with this Act`

-- "Shall respond" is the duty of the person inquired of; complied with when there was no inquiry under
-- subsection (1) or the person responded.
-- src:2932 | (2) A person shall respond to any inquiry made under subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 237(2) (src:2932)
GIVEN `an inquiry was made of the person under subsection 237(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person responded to the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has complied with the duty to respond within s 237(2)` IF
        (NOT `an inquiry was made of the person under subsection 237(1)`)
    OR  `the person responded to the inquiry`
